doc-gen4 itself ships no NOTICE file; this entry is lean-doc's own attribution.

**lean-doc is a derivative work of doc-gen4 and has been changed.** It is not a
clean-room reimplementation: doc-gen4's sources were read, and byte-identical
output was used as the acceptance oracle while the renderer and the extractor
were written. What changed is the whole architecture around them — a Lean
extractor that emits an IR, Rust that consumes it, incremental rebuilds, a
dependency map that links out to pinned upstream sources instead of
regenerating them, and a UI written from scratch. What did not change is the
set of rendering and extraction decisions, which are doc-gen4's.

lean-doc is not doc-gen4, is not endorsed by its authors, and its output is not
compatible with doc-gen4's as of milestone M7.

The files below are where the reproduction is closest — some transcribed
verbatim, some rewritten in Rust to preserve the output byte for byte, some
restructured to write an IR instead of HTML:

    extractor/Extract.lean
    crates/lean-doc-md/src/html.rs
    crates/lean-doc-md/src/escape.rs
    crates/lean-doc-render/src/code.rs
    crates/lean-doc-render/src/whitespace.rs
    crates/lean-doc-render/src/autolink.rs
    crates/lean-doc-render/assets/style.css   (the `.fn` and `.break_within` rules)

Test fixtures produced by running doc-gen4:

    crates/lean-doc-md/tests/data/docgen4-expected.json
    crates/lean-doc-render/tests/data/docgen4-linked-expected.json

A patch against doc-gen4's own sources, quoting them as diff context:

    benchmarks/doc-gen4-instrumentation.patch

lean-doc does not link doc-gen4. The extractor imports only `Lean`; the Rust
crates have no Lean dependency at all.

